PipeWire's cameras (the Camera portal's path) listed and opened safely while cameras come
and go, each with the id V4L2 gives it.

PipeWire's own thread adds and removes the cameras as they are plugged in and out, while
the device info and the capture module read the list from another thread without a lock:
they now read it with PipeWire's loop locked. A camera whose formats are not known yet
(just plugged in) is not listed until they are, as the first listing already left out
cameras without one. A camera PipeWire reaches through V4L2 carries its V4L2 bus
(api.v4l2.cap.bus_info), which the device info tells (V4l2BusInfo) so that the wrapper
can keep the id V4L2's own device info gives the camera. Without PipeWire's library the
session said so and then went on to use it; it now stops there.

